inson they  asked her to take off her helmet and  deliver the lines simple enough right  not simple for kravitz because she just  got too caught up in that simple action  she recalled that awkward moment where  she attempted to capture catwoman's  sexiness but just couldn't accomplish  that with the helmet removal of course  she was able to get the part but this  moment definitely made it harder for her  yeah i'm trying to be like i don't care  number three if only zoe knew that she  was not alone during this moment and  that the fearsome batman was having his  own panic attack alongside her i felt  like i was still alive yeah that was the  case for poor robert as this was also  his first time saying a single line as  the batman we can understand being a  little nervous with the cameras on you  for the first time in a new role but he  really wasn't even shown during  kravitz's screen test it's hard it's  hard it's it was a really large role  robert was even leaning on zoe for  emotional support during the scene and  she really did do well considering she  got the part maybe it was just the  nerves of saying the lines but we can  also agree that zoe's acting skills had  a part to catch robert off guard and she  like didn't look nervous at all she was  kind of improvising and stuff number  four there are times when actors just  have a hard time getting into their  roles but for pattinson all he had to do  was put on the suit i still can't really  understand that it's even happening the  history and legacy of the costume can  really work wonders on an actor's  performance changing everything from  their body to their voice you put the  suit on and you have to speak in a  certain way robert accredits a lot of  his performance to his bat suit with the  way it gives him a sort of strange power  and this kind of feeling can rub off on  others specifically the cast and crew  people get freaked out by it when he put  on the outfit for the first time for a  camera test robert could see the  frightened look on everyone's faces and  him being such a nice guy this was a  little tough to swallow for him but  feeling this kind of frightening power  in the batsuit isn't a new thing a lot  of batman actors shared similar stories  of donning the cape there are no reports  yet as to whether pattinson added his  method acting approach to the role but  maybe the suit just did it for him has  such a kind of totemic power number five  the villains of batman are almost  endless and putting together the look of  colin farrell's penguin for the film  seemed a little lengthy too someone to  do the teeth someone to do the wig  someone to do that there's something to  do we sat and wondered when we would see  penguin for the first time in the  trailer second guessing who exactly that  actor was and that's thanks to the  film's makeup department who worked  tirelessly with feral to get the look  down right it just sparked my  imagination and continued to every day  that i went to work it wasn't as  difficult as most processes are for  initial makeup designs and it was also a  very big team effort colin recalled  having a very enjoyable time working  endlessly with the other artists to get  a look that works for both the actor and  the film it was so exciting and we were  all just on the same page all this work  helped mold his character and voice  something that can definitely take the  load off an actor's busy schedule we're  more than excited to see a little more  of his character when the film comes out  and thinking just how they were able to  make a very recognizable actor  unrecognizable  number six even batman can rock some  heels and this one apparently needed  them seems like such a bad idea you know  pattinson six foot height wasn't enough  for director matt reeves so they opted  for some stylish high-heeled shoes  instead pattinson found them a little  ridiculous with the seriousness of the  character but they were adamant about  using them so of course he obliged i  wanted to do a radically different thing  to all the other batman the full outfit  reveal looked so batman to us and all  the aspects of its design definitely  played out well in the end for his  character but if they were a little too  awkward for robert to wear we wonder if  they had extra rehearsal time for him to  practice punching bad guys in heels  it's a it's a quite unusual dance  number seven the world's greatest  detective couldn't figure robert was  donning the cows so early on but leave  it to a batman visionary to see right  through him i hadn't told a soul about  it dark knight director christopher  nolan snagged pattinson for a role in  his film tenet and to his surprise  pattinson had just got secretly offered  the role of batman a day before shooting  began robert was told to be a little  hush-hush about the role initially but  somehow nolan has a hand in everything  batman chris obviously has the inside  scoop christopher confronted him the  first day after robert told a little fib  about a family emergency to go screen  test for matt reeves though no worries  nolan was just as happy for him as  pattinson was getting the role and to  get a congratulations from one of the  finest batman directors in cinema  history must have really meant a lot to  him  number eight there was a short period of  time after ben affleck left the titular  role that every actor wanted in on his  replacement and for pattinson curiosity  came to him when he met with the batman  producer dylan clark for a non-related  discussion i saw in his imdb that there  was just rumored batman involvement  pattinson always had an affinity for  batman and always wanted to be involved  in a superhero movie meeting with the  producer was his best chance so he  decided to give him a little push  towards his direction to think about  casting him there's an opening there so  i kind of kept pushing and pushing with  an open-ended twinkle in clark's eye he  definitely saw robert as a potential  candidate for the role just that small  question from pattinson started a  cascade of persuasion and insistence  from him to finally snag the part number  nine a surprising initial choice to play  the villain role of riddler was jonah  hill he was actually in deep  conversations with producers before  dropping the part we really couldn't  imagine why he dropped such a title role  but we can be glad it landed in  award-winning actor paul dano's hands  hill does indeed have a very impressive  acting resume and there's no doubt he  wouldn't have made the role  extraordinary in the new batman however  with the look we've gotten of the new  riddler from the trailers we simply  cannot wait to see dano's take on it  these actors really put in a lot of  effort and desire to audition for the  batman and casting did a great job  picking them if robert pattinson never  rocked those high-heeled shoes and the  outfit would he have still been right  for the role did you have a favorite  audition experience from the batman  let us know in the comments
 

